WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
Type sine of nought, over
nought, into a calculator.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.410
It says error.

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.060
Fair enough: you can't divide by nought.

4
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.000
But try x closer and closer
to nought, in radians,

5
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.430
and plot sine x over x.

6
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.820
The graph seems to be heading somewhere.

7
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.490
So what is it at x equals nought?

8
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.320
Nought?

9
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.750
Nothing at all?

10
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.420
In this mission, you'll meet limits: a
limit can exist even where a function is

11
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.760
undefined.

12
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.680
And you'll see why nought over
nought is an indeterminate form:

13
00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.730
the limit could be anything.

14
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: find what sine x over x is
heading for as x gets close to nought.
